{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Helvetica;}}\f0\fs24 {\b Topology}\par Numbers (Modify)\par Pages (Create)\par \par {\b Request}\par Last Thursday our payments API slowed down badly for about 40 minutes and a few percent of card payments timed out. I was the incident lead, and now I need to work out the real cause and write the postmortem. In Numbers I'll open the request log export, filter down to the failed and slow requests, and build a pivot table and a chart by minute, version and server to see where the problem actually was. I'll compare that against the deploy log and the release notes to find the change that caused it. Then in Pages I'll write the postmortem with the impact, a short timeline, the root cause and the follow-up actions with owners. Deliverables are the log analysis workbook and the postmortem as a PDF.\par \par {\b Task Description}\par 1. In Numbers, open the incident workbook and sort and filter the request log to the slow and timed out requests to find when the problem started and stopped.\par 2. In Numbers, build a pivot table of requests by app version, server and result to see which servers were affected.\par 3. In Numbers, build a pivot table of results by minute and add a line chart to show the shape of the incident.\par 4. In Numbers, compare the deploy log and the release notes with the chart to find the change that caused it, then export the workbook to Excel.\par 5. In Pages, fill in the postmortem template with the summary, customer impact, the missing timeline entries, the root cause and three follow-up actions with owners.\par 6. In Pages, export the postmortem as a PDF.\par }